\f0\fs24 \cf0 ### GlobalShiftMask.m\
\
GUI tool that globally shifts all ROI positions by a user-specified X/Y pixel offset and saves the result as a new maskObj .mat file. Does not perform bolus tracking.\
\
**Syntax:**\
```matlab\
GlobalShiftMask\
```\
\
**GUI buttons:**\
\
| Button | Function |\
|--------|----------|\
| Load Data | Load a bolus TIFF and display its MIP |\
| Import ROIs | Load a maskObj and overlay ROIs on the MIP (thin red lines, no blue dots) |\
| Pop-out View | Enter X/Y shift values, apply them, and display the shifted ROIs in a zoomable window for verification |\
| Save Mask | Save the shifted maskObj as a new .mat file |\
\
**How to use:**\
\
1. Click Load Data and select the bolus TIFF you want to check alignment against\
2. Click Import ROIs and select the maskObj file \'97 ROIs appear as red outlines on the MIP in the main window\
3. Click Pop-out View \'97 enter X and Y pixel shift values \'97 a new window shows the shifted ROIs overlaid on the MIP\
4. Zoom and pan to verify alignment\
5. If happy, click Save Mask in the main window\
6. If not happy, click Pop-out View again with different values\
\
**Shift value calculation:**\
\
If using Visual Studio registration, both bolus files are registered to the XYZ stack. The shift to apply to the ROIs is:\
\
```\
X shift = dx_B - dx_A\
Y shift = dy_B - dy_A\
```\
\
where A is the bolus the ROIs were drawn on, and B is the other bolus in the pair. Positive X = rightward; positive Y = downward.\
\
**Output:** A .mat file containing a `maskObj` struct array with `.Position` fields, compatible with BolusTrack's "Import ROIs" button.\
}